Good Afternoon,

=20

Yet another lovely weather day in South Carolina on this fine Thursday.  =
We
hope you are all having a GREAT week!

=20

Here is a photo from our flying adventure to the Runway Caf=E9 at the
Greenville Downtown Airport yesterday.  From left to right:  Bill Como, =
Dick
Hitt, Steve Sanderson, Lara Kaufmann, Steve Crimm, Ken Plesser, Don =
Cook.
Lara is the Public Relations Director at the airport and added some much
needed beauty to our table, not to mention lowering the average age
considerably.

=20



=20

=20

Our joke today comes from our friends at Clean Laffs.

=20

Keep smiling=85=85=85=85=85=85=85=85=85=85=85=85=85..ss

=20

*************************************************************************=
***
********************************************************

=20

                                                REPAIRS NEEDED

=20

When the icemaker in our new refrigerator broke, my husband dropped by =
the
store to arrange for repairs. Because the sun was bright, my husband's =
eyes
hadn't adjusted to the dim light inside in time to see a woman sitting =
on
the floor examining carpet samples.

=20

He stepped on her leg and she screamed, causing him to jump into a =
display
of fireplace tools that went crashing in every direction. Unnerved, my
husband stumbled over to the service desk, and as he went to rest his =
hands
on the counter, he flipped over a bowl full of little mints, scattering =
them
everywhere.

=20

After taking a deep breath to calm himself, he announced to the =
wide-eyed
woman working there, "My refrigerator doesn't work."

=20

"I don't doubt it," she replied.

=20

=20

Steve Sanderson

Gilbert, South Carolina 29054

aardvark@illinois.edu

 <http://www.facebook.com/steve.sanderson2>
http://www.facebook.com/steve.sanderson2

=20


